==Mechanics==
A Tenet variant of a weapon will only provide [[Mastery Rank]] points once. A second weapon of the same variant but with a different Sister name will not provide extra mastery.

===[[Weapons#Overleveling|Overleveling]]===
{{Transclude|Weapons#Overleveling}}

===Elemental Bonus===

The Tenet weapons additionally have bonus damage of one damage type which can either be {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, or {{D|Radiation}}, ranging from 25-60% of the weapon's '''base damage''' determined randomly, with lower percentages being more common.<ref name="drop_chance_data">https://www.reddit.com/r/Warframe/comments/dz0tze/kuva_lich_data_weapon_drop_rates_elemental_bonus/</ref> The damage type of this bonus damage is determined by the Progenitor Warframe, as per [[Adversary System/Progenitor|this table]]. For store-bought Tenet weapons, the damage type is randomly generated when Ergo Glast's shop refreshes. This additional bonus damage applies as weapon base damage, meaning elemental mods and status that scale from base / modified base damage will be affected.

A rank 40 Tenet weapon can be applied with an {{Resource|Elemental Vice}} that enables the Valence Override option, which allows swapping between the bonus damage types freely. This does not affect the damage percentage.

===[[Valence Fusion]]===
{{Transclude|Valence Fusion#Adversary Weapons}}
{{Transclude|Valence Fusion#Extra Math}}

==Notes==
*Unclaimed Tenet weapons in the Foundry can be sold directly for {{cc|10,000}}.
*Tenet weapons need to be Rank 40 in order to be Entitled, whereas [[Kuva (Variant)|Kuva Weapons]] can be Entitled at Rank 30.
*The total number of Tenet weapons is 16, requiring 80 {{Resource|Forma}} to max rank them all.

==Trivia==
*When [[holster]]ed, {{Weapon|Tenet Envoy}}, {{Weapon|Tenet Diplos}}, {{Weapon|Tenet Grigori}}, and {{Weapon|Tenet Livia}} fold up into an attaché case.
*Non-Tenet variants of the {{Weapon|Tenet Agendus}} and {{Weapon|Tenet Spirex}}, wielded by [[Crewman#Juno Crewman|Juno Crewmen]], [[Comba#Juno Comba|Juno Combas]], and [[Zerca]]s, are exclusive to those enemies and not obtainable for players.
*Tenet is an English word meaning a principle, belief, or doctrine generally held to be true.<ref name="merriam-webster dictionary">https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/tenet</ref>
*Tenet in Latin means: maintain, sustain, conserve, possess and domain.

